        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "<i>K</i><sub>p</sub> is the product of the equilibrium partial pressures of the products over those of the reactants, each raised to the power of its coefficient in the equation: <i>K</i><sub>p</sub> = <i>p</i><sup>2</sup>SO<sub>3</sub> / (<i>p</i><sup>2</sup>SO<sub>2</sub> × <i>p</i>O<sub>2</sub>).",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:7.1(6)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "The Contact process runs at only about 1–2 atm. A higher pressure would raise the equilibrium yield slightly (3 mol of gas → 2 mol), but the conversion is already high at low pressure with a V<sub>2</sub>O<sub>5</sub> catalyst at about 450 °C, so the extra cost of high-pressure plant is not justified. About 200 atm is the pressure associated with the Haber process.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:7.1(10)"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "optionAnalysis": [
            {
              "key": "A",
              "correct": true,
              "text": "Correct. Products over reactants with coefficients as powers, and the Contact process operates at about 2 atm."
            },
            {
              "key": "B",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "The pressure is right but the expression is upside down (reactants over products)."
            },
            {
              "key": "C",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "The expression is right but 200 atm is the Haber process pressure, not the Contact process."
            },
            {
              "key": "D",
              "correct": false,
              "text": "Both wrong: the expression is inverted and the pressure is that of the Haber process."
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Write <i>K</i><sub>p</sub> as products over reactants: <i>p</i><sup>2</sup>SO<sub>3</sub> / (<i>p</i><sup>2</sup>SO<sub>2</sub> × <i>p</i>O<sub>2</sub>), which rules out B and D.",
            "Recall the Contact process conditions: about 1–2 atm, 450 °C, V<sub>2</sub>O<sub>5</sub> catalyst, which rules out C.",
            "Answer A."
